{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB12459 - MONDO_20543",
  "verbalization": "Belotecan shows a strong association with Theca Steroid-producing Cell Malignant Tumor Of Ovary, Not Further Specified through three distinct but related pathways. In all three paths, Belotecan is linked to a malignant germ cell tumor of the ovary, which in turn is associated with Melphalan or Tretamine, both of which are known to target the theca cell lineage. The presence of Melphalan and Tretamine in these pathways suggests a potential shared mechanism of action involving the theca steroid-producing cells, possibly through the inhibition of specific enzymes or signaling pathways critical to their function. The high scores in all three paths indicate a consistent and significant relationship, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Belotecan may have a role in targeting the theca cell lineage in this tumor type, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct therapeutic effect.",
